      "name": "Why Indoor Air Can Get Worse",
      "char_file": "미세먼지_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The EPA's wildfire smoke",
        "guidance actually flips",
        "a lot of the usual advice",
        "",
        "Three habits make indoor air",
        "worse on bad air days"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cracking the Windows Open",
      "char_file": "창문_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Opening windows during a",
        "smoke event or pollution alert",
        "",
        "lets outdoor particles",
        "straight into your home"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Switch to Recirculate Mode",
      "char_file": "창문_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Switch your HVAC fan to",
        "recirculate mode instead",
        "",
        "Swap in a MERV-13 filter",
        "if your system can handle it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Frying, Broiling, and Candles",
      "char_file": "프라이팬_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Cooking indoors pushes",
        "particle levels far higher",
        "than what's happening outside",
        "",
        "It can take over an hour",
        "for levels to clear"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cook Later or Run the Hood",
      "char_file": "프라이팬_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Cook after air quality",
        "improves if you can",
        "",
        "Or run your range hood",
        "on high the whole time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Running the Vacuum",
      "char_file": "청소기_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Vacuuming stirs settled",
        "dust right back into",
        "the air you're breathing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Run a Real HEPA Purifier",
      "char_file": "공기청정기_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Skip the vacuum until",
        "levels drop",
        "",
        "Run a properly sized HEPA",
        "purifier that makes",
        "little to no ozone"
      ]
    }
